message: "If you use this dataset, please cite it using the metadata in this file."
title: "An economic geography panel of U.S. county-level labor and skill demand, 2010-2024"
abstract: >-
  A publicly available county-year panel of U.S. labor and skill demand,
  derived from 433.6 million Lightcast (formerly Burning Glass) job postings
  spanning 2010-2024. The panel covers 3,194 counties across 15 years
  (47,891 county-year observations) and reports 137 variables organized into
  twelve groups: a 44-variable headline subset describing the volume,
  employer-entity composition, skill content, specialization, complexity,
  relatedness, and dynamics of local labor demand, plus 93 additional
  variables for employer-pair skill-similarity, per-employer-type dynamics,
  and extended work-mode analyses intended for spillover and decomposition
  research.
